{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"ecosystem/agent-frameworks","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Agent Frameworks","objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Say what an agent framework gives you, and that you do not strictly need one","Recognise the main names: LangChain, LangGraph, deepagents, CrewAI and n8n","Tell a workflow apart from an agent, and know when the workflow is the better choice"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[],"previous":{"key":"expert/advanced-llm-evaluation","number":34,"title":"Advanced LLM Evaluation","drawn":false,"track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"ecosystem/inference-providers","number":36,"title":"Inference Providers","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"what-a-framework-gives-you","text":"What a Framework Gives You","depth":2},{"id":"the-langchain-stack","text":"The LangChain Stack","depth":2},{"id":"the-other-python-options","text":"The Other Python Options","depth":2},{"id":"ai-workflows","text":"AI Workflows","depth":2},{"id":"no-code-options","text":"No-code Options","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"-articles","text":"📄 Articles","depth":3},{"id":"️-tools","text":"🛠️ Tools","depth":3},{"id":"️-repositories","text":"🗃️ Repositories","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything up to here was about how agents work. This module is a map of what people actually use when they build one. You will hear these names in meetings and from vendors."}],"lead":true},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"When a team or a vendor proposes an AI project, they will name a framework or a platform. You do not need to install any of them. But knowing what each one is for helps you follow the discussion and ask the right question, which is often: \"does this need an agent at all, or would a fixed workflow do?\""}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-framework-gives-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What a Framework Gives You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"You do not strictly need a framework. "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" showed that the agent loop is simple. A framework is the ready-made plumbing around that loop:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"trying again when an AI service fails for a moment"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"showing the answer word by word as it is written"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"describing tools in a standard way"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"remembering things after a restart"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"keeping the traces from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/observability","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Observability"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"It is like buying a ready-made kitchen instead of building every cupboard yourself. That is why most teams stop writing their own loop after their second project."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-langchain-stack","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The LangChain Stack"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the name you will hear most often. It is the most complete, and the one most likely to be in use near you. \"LangChain\" is really three layers:"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"35.1","title":"The LangChain Stack","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/ab08a3298d2fd58982eb2c0ef0f97161.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/8847ecb12e2764a16a667596ffd51e89.svg"}},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/langgraph-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"LangGraph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the lowest layer, for teams that want full control over each step."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/langchain.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"LangChain"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the main layer, and where most teams start."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/deepagents.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"deepagents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the top layer: the deep agent from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/context-engineering","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Context Engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":", with planning, helpers, notes and summarising already built in."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-other-python-options","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Other Python Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"They do the same job with different trade-offs:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/crewai.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"CrewAI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" organises agents as a crew of roles, the team idea from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/multi-agent","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Multi-Agent Systems"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/huggingface.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"smolagents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from Hugging Face is small on purpose and easy to read."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/agno.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Agno"}]},{"type":"text","text":" focuses on running and managing many agents as one system."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/pydantic.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Pydantic AI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" focuses on strict checking, so mistakes show up as clear errors."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/mastra-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"Mastra"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/voltagent.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"VoltAgent"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are for companies whose product is written in TypeScript rather than Python."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ai-workflows","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI Workflows"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the most useful distinction in the module, and choosing wrong can cost months."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI workflow"}]},{"type":"text","text":" follows steps that someone wrote down, like a company procedure. The steps are fixed. The AI is used inside some steps, for one job each. An "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI agent"}]},{"type":"text","text":" decides the steps itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The mistake is to think the agent is the better, grown-up version. It is not. When you know the steps and they rarely change, a workflow is more predictable, cheaper, and easier to fix when something breaks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/n8n.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"n8n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the tool most teams choose for workflows. You build them on a visual canvas by connecting boxes, it connects to more than 400 services, and it can run on the company's own computers. Take a job like: \"when a form is submitted, sort it, look something up, save it to the database, and send a message.\" For that job, a workflow is easily better than an agent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"And the two now work together. n8n can be connected to a coding agent through MCP (from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":"). You describe the workflow in plain words, and the agent builds it in n8n, tests it and fixes what broke. The agent becomes the thing that writes the workflow."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"no-code-options","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"No-code Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"For many jobs, the right answer is a no-code platform. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://lovable.dev/"},"inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/lovable.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Lovable"}]}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://bolt.new/"},"inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/bolt-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"Bolt"}]}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://replit.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/replit.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Replit"}]}]},{"type":"text","text":" turn a description into a working app, put it online, and let you keep changing it with more requests. For a prototype, an internal tool or a simple page with a form, that takes hours instead of weeks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: you get speed now and less control later. If you ever move off the platform, you build the app again. Know which of those you are buying."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework"}]},{"type":"text","text":": ready-made software around the agent loop."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LangChain / LangGraph / deepagents"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the three layers of the most common framework family."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI workflow"}]},{"type":"text","text":": fixed steps someone wrote, with AI inside some of them."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"n8n"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the most common workflow tool, built visually."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"No-code platform"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a service that builds a working app from a description."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A framework is the plumbing around the agent loop, and LangChain is the name you will hear most. But the most important question is often not which framework: it is whether you need an agent at all. When the steps are known, a workflow (often in n8n) is cheaper and more predictable, and an agent can now build that workflow for you. For simple apps, a no-code platform may be enough."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": When is a workflow a better choice than an agent? And what do you give up with a no-code platform?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-articles","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"📄 Articles"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.promptingguide.ai/agents/ai-workflows-vs-ai-agents"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AI Workflows vs AI Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the distinction, and when each one is right"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🛠️ Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://lovable.dev/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Lovable"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://bolt.new/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Bolt"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://replit.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Replit"}]},{"type":"text","text":": describe an app in plain language and get a working one"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-repositories","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🗃️ Repositories"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LangChain"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the main framework, and the place most teams start"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CrewAI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": agents organised as roles in a crew"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"n8n"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the visual workflow platform"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":null}